public static int Sum(int x, int y)
{
    for (int i = 0; i < y; i++){
        x.Inc(1);
    }
    Debug.Assert(OLD(x) + y == x);
    return x;
}
```

The assert statement is added to make sure the value of x increases by y in the function. This is verified by comparing the old value of x with the value x is updated to after the loop. If the assert statement is true, the program will continue execution. If it is false, the program will throw an AssertionException.

